From: CB1 Batocera POC <cb1-poc@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: add CB1 SD Batocera POC with built-in HDMI

The already patched CB1 dtsi enables de, hdmi, hdmi_out and gpu. The CB1
SD source in Armbian sunxi-7.2 only adds properties to disabled optional
peripherals; no such overlays are needed here. Restore the original CB1
GPU supply (DCDC1, vdd-gpu-sys). Enable only the H616 AHUB platform and
HDMI machine nodes used by the Orange Pi Zero HDMI sound path.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h616-bigtreetech-cb1-batocera.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-a64-amarula-relic.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-a64-bananapi-m64.dtb
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-bigtreetech-cb1-batocera.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-bigtreetech-cb1-batocera.dts
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-bigtreetech-cb1-batocera.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0+ or MIT)
+/* Experimental CB1 SD + Pi4B Adapter image; never apply the TFT overlay. */
+/dts-v1/;
+
+#include "sun50i-h616-bigtreetech-cb1.dtsi"
+
+&gpu {
+	mali-supply = <&reg_dcdc1>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&ahub_dam_plat {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&ahub1_plat {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&ahub1_mach {
+	status = "okay";
+};
